    "rationale": [
      "ANA-A07 forbids an implicit global maxLagSeconds; this candidate binds the value only to the eight explicit ANA-A09 funnel metrics.",
      "The only already-certified operational ANA publication cadence is the 300-second canonical window plus a 60-second projection-delay budget used by ANA-A11. Reusing that cadence as a candidate baseline avoids inventing a second arbitrary analytics cadence; it does not inherit ANA-A11 runtime authority.",
      "All eight funnel metrics are produced by one canonical A09 compute RPC, so one threshold avoids contradictory freshness states within the same projection batch.",
      "The cross-domain quote_submitted_to_order_requested metric already uses min(windowEnd, behaviorWatermark, orderWatermark) as dataThrough. Dependency lag is therefore represented in dataThrough and must not be double-counted by adding a second ORD-specific lag allowance.",
      "A 360-second threshold permits one full five-minute canonical window plus sixty seconds for projection after dataThrough. Any older fully covered snapshot becomes stale; missing policy or unavailable coverage remains unavailable."
    ],
    "dependencyLagDoubleCounted": false,
    "a11AuthorityInherited": false,
    "futureCadenceChangeRequiresNewRevision": true
  },
